WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.195 --> 00:00:14.255
was brought up to the deck of the Jolly Roger.

2
00:00:15.556 --> 00:00:18.776
The boys were lined up in their chains trying to look brave.

3
00:00:20.377 --> 00:00:24.358
When she saw the pirates preparing the plank, she was filled with hate.

4
00:00:25.638 --> 00:00:28.439
She hated Hook and she hated the pirates.

5
00:00:29.799 --> 00:00:33.421
Boys might think pirates exciting, but Wendy did not.

6
00:00:35.382 --> 00:00:38.704
She especially hated that the ship had not been cleaned for years.

7
00:00:40.025 --> 00:00:42.666
Not one window was without a layer of grime.

8
00:00:43.847 --> 00:00:49.230
In fact, while she was below, she wrote "Dirty Pig" on a window with her finger.

9
00:00:50.771 --> 00:00:54.293
She also hated that it was nighttime and no one was in bed.

10
00:00:56.054 --> 00:00:59.876
But when the boys gathered around her, all these thoughts melted away.

11
00:01:01.500 --> 00:01:07.743
"So, my beauty," said Hook, "soon you will see your children walk the plank."

12
00:01:08.943 --> 00:01:13.865
Hook's lace collar was dirty, and when he saw Wendy staring, he tried to hide it.

13
00:01:13.885 --> 00:01:17.047
"Are the children going to die?"

14
00:01:17.707 --> 00:01:19.148
she asked scornfully.

15
00:01:20.468 --> 00:01:23.710
Her voice made it clear how she despised Hook for his plan.

16
00:01:23.730 --> 00:01:25.591
"They are!"

17
00:01:26.211 --> 00:01:26.771
he shouted.

18
00:01:26.791 --> 00:01:31.841
"Silence! Listen to a mother's last words to her children."

19
00:01:33.741 --> 00:01:36.822
Wendy stood tall and faced everyone proudly.

20
00:01:36.842 --> 00:01:41.043
"These are my last words, dear boys," she said.

21
00:01:41.063 --> 00:01:48.065
"I feel that your real mothers would say this: We hope our sons die like gentlemen."

22
00:01:49.566 --> 00:01:50.626
Hook shuddered.

23
00:01:52.067 --> 00:01:56.948
Even the pirates were awed, for Wendy's words were the kind that inspired bravery.

24
00:01:58.112 --> 00:02:02.354
Tootles cried out, "I am going to do what my mother wishes.

25
00:02:03.214 --> 00:02:04.995
What are you going to do, Slightly?"

26
00:02:05.015 --> 00:02:09.517
"What my mother wishes," said Slightly.

27
00:02:09.537 --> 00:02:11.998
"What are you going to do, Nibs?"

28
00:02:13.158 --> 00:02:18.201
Nibs answered the same way, and so did the other boys until Hook interrupted.

29
00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:20.502
"Tie her up to the mast!"

30
00:02:21.262 --> 00:02:22.742
he shouted cruelly.

31
00:02:24.563 --> 00:02:26.024
It was Smee who tied Wendy.

32
00:02:27.112 --> 00:02:32.075
Under his breath, he whispered, "I'll save you if you promise to be my mother."

33
00:02:33.416 --> 00:02:36.518
But this was a promise Wendy could never make to a pirate.

34
00:02:37.779 --> 00:02:42.622
The boys' eyes had drifted from Wendy to the plank, and their faces went white.

35
00:02:44.584 --> 00:02:46.085
They were not ready to die.

36
00:02:47.165 --> 00:02:52.769
Their walk down the narrow board and over the end into the cold sea would be the last

37
00:02:52.869 --> 00:02:54.230
walk they would ever take.

38
00:02:55.391 --> 00:02:59.865
They shivered and stared, no longer sure they could walk the plank as gentlemen.

39
00:03:01.046 --> 00:03:04.107
They were, after all, only little boys.

40
00:03:05.828 --> 00:03:08.289
Hook smiled and took a step toward Wendy.

41
00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:13.011
He wanted to turn her face to make her watch the boys walk the plank.

42
00:03:14.211 --> 00:03:16.972
He wanted to hear her cries of terror and regret.

43
00:03:18.093 --> 00:03:21.994
Instead, what he heard filled his own heart with terror.

44
00:03:23.195 --> 00:03:25.496
It was the tick-tock of the crocodile.

45
00:03:27.232 --> 00:03:32.397
They all heard it—Hook, the other pirates, the boys, and Wendy.

46
00:03:33.718 --> 00:03:38.542
Instantly, they all looked—but not at the water where the sound was coming from.

47
00:03:39.883 --> 00:03:42.265
All their eyes were fixed on Captain Hook.

48
00:03:43.306 --> 00:03:48.190
The crocodile, Hook knew, had only one victim in mind—him!

49
00:03:49.311 --> 00:03:51.833
He fell to the floor, trembling in a heap.

50
00:03:53.375 --> 00:03:57.114
The ticking grew louder, as if the crocodile were getting closer.

51
00:03:58.195 --> 00:04:02.918
Hook crawled on his knees to the other side of the ship, away from the boys and Wendy.

52
00:04:03.679 --> 00:04:05.921
The awful sound was getting even louder.

53
00:04:07.142 --> 00:04:11.705
All Hook could imagine was the terrible crocodile climbing aboard his ship.

54
00:04:11.725 --> 00:04:14.127
"Hide me!"

55
00:04:14.728 --> 00:04:18.291
Hook cried, but his men stepped back to clear the way.

56
00:04:19.412 --> 00:04:25.172
They had always been loyal to their captain, but none of them would stand between him and his

57
00:04:25.292 --> 00:04:30.914
fate. On the other side of the deck, the boys leaned over the side of the ship to

58
00:04:30.974 --> 00:04:32.435
see the crocodile climb in.

59
00:04:33.535 --> 00:04:37.597
But to their surprise, it was not the crocodile coming to their rescue.

60
00:04:38.897 --> 00:04:39.718
It was Peter!

61
00:04:40.818 --> 00:04:42.659
He made a sign for them to keep silent.

62
00:04:43.319 --> 00:04:45.180
Then he went on ticking.
